  "title": "Enhanced Feedback & Tool Visibility Controls",
  "summary": "Discovery Engine now supports detailed feedback on Model Armor verdicts and response quality. New schemas also introduce fine-grained visibility controls for internal tools and allow specifying Identity Provider configurations during project provisioning.",
  "details": "Developers can now provide more granular feedback on response quality via new enum values in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFeedback.reasons`: `RELEVANT`, `COMPREHENSIVE`, `GOOD_CITATION`, and `ACCURATE`. A significant addition is the `modelArmorDisputeInfo` field to the `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFeedback` schema, referencing the new `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaFeedbackModelArmorDisputeInfo` schema. This enables users to dispute Model Armor `BLOCK` or `FLAG` verdicts, providing `expectedLabel`, `sanitizationResultJson`, and `templateName`.\n\nNew schemas `ApiservingMcpMcpToolVisibility` and `ApiservingMcpMcpToolVisibilityFieldVisibility` have been introduced, allowing for detailed control over tool and field visibility, including a `visibilityEnforcementStrategy` (though noted as \"DO NOT USE\" for now). Finally, the `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaProvisionProjectRequest` now accepts an optional `idpConfig` to configure Identity Providers during project setup, influencing ACLs.",
  "impact": "medium",
